  "prefLabel": "Ncr 532.02 Permission Required to Exceed 50 Percent Basal Area",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ncr 532.02 Permission Required to Exceed 50 Percent Basal Area. Permission from the director shall be required to remove more than 50 percent of the basal area from a well distributed stand of healthy growing trees within areas specified by RSA 227‑J:9, I. At least 30 days prior to commencing cutting operations, a landowner or authorized agent shall apply for permission to exceed 50 percent basal area by completing and submitting Form 532a, as described in Ncr 532.03.\n\nSource. #14243, INTERIM, eff 4-23-25; ss by #14452 (formerly Ncr 5302.02), eff 12-6-25, EXPIRES 12-6-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ncr520-590.html"
